PUBLIC RESPONSE: I-II-VI

The shared plot-central element is a homophonic dying-message/wordplay clue: Christie’s “pile of carp” points to “pilocarpine,” and Asimov’s “The Next Day” turns on “tomorrow”/“Morrow”-type sound ambiguity. To translate such a clue, one can:
- I: transcreate with an analogous target-language pun;
- II: provide English audio so readers can hear the original phonetic clue;
- VI: add footnotes with phonetic transcriptions explaining the original sound-play.

Changing the setting, adding a foreign accent, or including an illustration would not by itself preserve a verbal homophone.

